<p>Follow the procedure below to print an image superimposed on prints. 
 The image is referred to as a watermark.</p>
<p>A watermark made up of a bitmap file (extension .bmp) is referred to 
 as an image watermark.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If you use this function, register the image watermarks 
 in advance.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2>Having Images Stamped on Prints</h2>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Add Bitmap</span> 
 check box. Click <span class="Term-Soft">Edit...</span> to open a dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Enter a name for a new watermark in the <span class="Term-Soft">Name:</span> box.<br/>
 To edit a registered watermark, select the watermark in the <span class="Term-Soft">Bitmap:</span> 
 list.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="5">
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Path/File Name:</span> 
 box, specify the path and file name for the bitmap data. Alternatively, 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Browse...</span> to select the bitmap data you want 
 to use.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the position where you want to print the 
 watermark in the <span class="Term-Soft">Position:</span> list.</p></li>
<li><p>To adjust the size for the watermark, specify 
 a value in the <span class="Term-Soft">Size:</span> spin box.</p></li>
<li><p>To print the watermark on the first page only, 
 select the <span class="Term-Soft">First Page Only</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>To place the watermark over the document, select 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Opaque</span> check box. The document under 
 the watermark will not be visible.</p></li>
<li><p>To print watermarks repeatedly, select the <span class="Term-Soft">Repeat</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>To print watermarks on each original page when 
 Layout or Booklet setting is applied, select the <span class="Term-Soft">Per 
 Original Page</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>After specifying the settings, click<span class="Term-Soft"> 
 Add</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">Update</span> to save the watermark.<br/>
 If you click <span class="Term-Soft">Update</span>, a dialog box appears 
 asking if you want to overwrite the old watermark. Click <span class="Term-Soft">Yes</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">You can select 
 the registered image watermark in the <span class="Term-Soft">Bitmap:</span> 
 list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> menu.</p></li>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">To print the 
 same watermark data using different setting configurations, provide each 
 of the available data combinations with its own watermark data name and 
 register those names in advance.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<h2>Deleting an Image Watermark</h2>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Add Bitmap</span> 
 check box. Click <span class="Term-Soft">Edit...</span> to open a dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select a watermark from the <span class="Term-Soft">Bitmap:</span> 
 list, and then click <span class="Term-Soft">Delete</span>. </p></li>
<li><p>A dialog box appears prompting for confirmation. 
 Click <span class="Term-Soft">Yes</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
